1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,433
real2simcapture is now open source: a capture and asset pipeline for robotics developers. This video shows actual code and workflow, not a physical-device scanning demonstration.

2
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:20,300
The native capture code records images, depth, camera poses and intrinsics. Capture requires compatible hardware; missing depth is never a substitute for LiDAR data.

3
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:29,800
The Live path periodically uploads mesh snapshots reconstructed by ARKit. Sampled frames are retained locally during network backlog. Device latency still requires measurement.

4
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:39,633
The workbench shows capture status, mesh versions and processing tasks. This is an actual empty workbench, with no fabricated scan result.

5
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:52,067
Export code supports MJCF, URDF and USD, with separate visual and collision geometry. Estimated mass and friction are not measurements. Outputs require target-engine acceptance.

6
00:00:52,067 --> 00:01:04,800
Source is available under Apache-2.0. Explore the code and contribute. This remains a developer preview: device signing, continuous capture and engine import await acceptance. No signed installable app is distributed.
